H("Conclusions")
P("A journal's recent acceptance times are a useful but over-confident forecast of its next papers. Estimating the cohort-to-cohort shift from earlier complete cohorts and widening the forecast accordingly improves calibration modestly and consistently in a strictly out-of-time evaluation and transfers to external journals against empirical quantiles, though not clearly against constant width inflation. Evaluations of turnaround forecasts should treat slow papers explicitly, and turnaround statistics should be reported as quantiles for explicit cohorts with uncertainty.")
